From ffa3cd8bd14ab8b6b612d957fce63b435325f2e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@soprasteria.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 22:14:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: test the light beam's panel-edge rule against the row
 on the panel

borg_light_beam() refuses to cast north or south "on the edge of
shifting the panel", but it compared the Borg's absolute dungeon row
with the panel height instead of its row on the panel. With a 22-row map
panel a north or south beam was therefore only ever cast in the top 21
rows of the dungeon, whatever part of the map was on screen. Subtract
the panel offset first, as the shift-panel code in borg-fight-defend.c
does.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#88.

(cherry picked from commit 828318ab58cbedc3f90cfe1a343ebd314257933b)
---
 src/borg/borg-light.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-light.c b/src/borg/borg-light.c
index 13f50db6d..45059d582 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-light.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-light.c
@@ -818,9 +818,9 @@ bool borg_light_beam(bool simulation)
     /* Don't do it if on the edge of shifting the panel. */
     if (dir == 5 || spell_ok == false || blocked == true
         || (dir == 2
-            && (borg.c.y > borg_panel_hgt() - 2))
+            && (borg.c.y - Term->offset_y > borg_panel_hgt() - 2))
         || (dir == 8
-            && (borg.c.y > borg_panel_hgt() - 2)))
+            && (borg.c.y - Term->offset_y > borg_panel_hgt() - 2)))
         return false;
 
     /* simulation */
-- 
